  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: aea490f53db83604eae9c1658210a5b5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  tutorialKey: tut_idlebattles_v1
  autoOpenOnEnable: 0
  pages:
  - icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5b05ebb3f339e4f03b3026941ea99ecc, type: 3}
    text: Idle Battles are now available. You can set a separate Idle Loadout in
      the Directory.
  - icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5b05ebb3f339e4f03b3026941ea99ecc, type: 3}
    text: Your Active Team is used for normal battles. Your Idle Loadout is used
      for idle rewards and offline activity.
  - icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5b05ebb3f339e4f03b3026941ea99ecc, type: 3}
    text: Use the Idle button in the Directory to switch views. When Idle is shown,
      you are editing idle slots. When Active is shown, you are editing your main
      team.
  - icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5b05ebb3f339e4f03b3026941ea99ecc, type: 3}
    text: Assigning a Bitling while Idle is active places it in the idle team. Assigning
      while Active is selected places it in the main team. A Bitling cannot be in
      both.
  - icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5b05ebb3f339e4f03b3026941ea99ecc, type: 3}
    text: If no Idle Loadout is set, your Active Team will be used automatically.
